   "Saint Charbel Makhlouf": 1,
   "Saint Charbel Makhlouf (1828-1898) was a Lebanese Maronite monk and hermit. He lived the last 23 years of his life in a hermitage near Annaya and died on December 24, 1898. Pope Paul VI canonized him on October 9, 1977. His feast is July 24, and people pray to him for healing.": 1,
