   "Frequently Asked Questions": 1,
   "Who was Saint Charbel?": 1,
   "A Lebanese Maronite monk and hermit, born Youssef Makhlouf on May 8, 1828. He died on December 24, 1898, and Pope Paul VI canonized him on October 9, 1977.": 1,
   "When is Saint Charbel's feast day?": 1,
   "July 24 in the Roman calendar, and the third Sunday of July in the Maronite calendar.": 1,
   "Where is Saint Charbel buried?": 1,
   "At the Monastery of Saint Maron in Annaya, Lebanon. See": 1,
   "the tomb": 1,
   "how to visit": 1,
   "Why is Saint Charbel called a wonderworker?": 1,
   "Because of the favors reported after his death. The Church formally approved miracles for his beatification and canonization, and the monastery keeps a wider register, which is not the same thing.": 1,
   "Is Saint Charbel the same as Saint Sharbel?": 1,
   "Yes. Charbel and Sharbel are two spellings of the same name, from Arabic.": 1,
